question:
What is the output of the following Java snippet?

int count = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) continue;
    count += i;
}
System.out.println(count);

What does this recursive function return for foo(4)?

int foo(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * foo(n - 1);
}

What is the output of the following C++ code?

int a = 5, b = 10;
int *p = &a;
*p = 20;
p = &b;
*p = 30;
cout << a << " " << b;

What is printed to console in the following closure example?

for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}

